<!-- ============ STORY ============ -->
<section class="section" id="story">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">My Story</div>
      <h2>From Bangladesh to Britain</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="story-quote">"I carried books before I carried ambition. The ambition came later — the questions were always there."</p>
        <div class="story-copy">
          <p>I grew up in Bangladesh with a habit that never left me: reading everything I could, and asking why things were the way they were.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <p>My working life began in <strong>customer service</strong>, where I learned that most problems are really about people feeling unheard. That grew into <strong>hospitality leadership</strong>, where I learned to run rooms, manage pressure, and lead people toward a shared standard of care.</p>
          <p>Coming to the <strong>United Kingdom for my education</strong> gave me the space to think differently. From there came <strong>entrepreneurship</strong> — building something of my own, shaped by everything I'd learned about people and systems.</p>
          <p>The most recent chapter is <strong>technology and productivity</strong> — helping professionals reclaim time through thoughtful AI systems.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="timeline">
          <li><span class="yr">Origin</span><div><div class="tt">Bangladesh</div><div class="td">Curiosity, books, and early questions about how the world works.</div></div></li>
          <li><span class="yr">Career</span><div><div class="tt">Customer Service &amp; Hospitality Leadership</div><div class="td">Learning people, pressure, and the discipline of consistent standards.</div></div></li>
          <li><span class="yr">Education</span><div><div class="tt">United Kingdom</div><div class="td">A new lens on learning, systems, and independent thinking.</div></div></li>
          <li><span class="yr">Building</span><div><div class="tt">Entrepreneurship</div><div class="td">Creating something of my own, shaped by every prior chapter.</div></div></li>
          <li><span class="yr">Today</span><div><div class="tt">Technology &amp; Productivity</div><div class="td">Helping professionals reclaim time through thoughtful AI systems.</div></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ BELIEFS ============ -->
<section class="section section-dim" id="beliefs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;text-align:center;">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center;">What I Believe</div>
      <h2>A short manifesto</h2>
      <p style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">Five convictions that guide how I write, build, and teach.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="beliefs-grid">
      <div class="belief-card reveal"><span class="belief-num">I</span><h4>Technology should serve humanity.</h4><p>Every tool I teach exists to give people back something human — attention, time, presence — never to replace it.</p></div>
      <div class="belief-card reveal reveal-delay-1"><span class="belief-num">II</span><h4>Productivity should create freedom, not burnout.</h4><p>Efficiency that leaves you more exhausted has failed at its only job.</p></div>
      <div class="belief-card reveal reveal-delay-2"><span class="belief-num">III</span><h4>Learning is a lifelong responsibility.</h4><p>The moment you decide you've learned enough is the moment you start falling behind.</p></div>
      <div class="belief-card reveal"><span class="belief-num">IV</span><h4>Stories shape societies.</h4><p>What we write and repeat quietly determines what a society believes is normal.</p></div>
      <div class="belief-card reveal reveal-delay-1"><span class="belief-num">V</span><h4>Success means being present for the people who matter.</h4><p>No achievement is worth much if it costs the attention people closest to you deserve.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

